1 0 0 1 62 730 Tm
(User Access Management Procedure) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Document Owner: Platform Operations) Tj
T*
(Last Reviewed: 2026-02-10) Tj
T*
(Applies To: Production systems operated by Platform Operations) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This procedure describes how the Platform Operations team requests, grants, reviews, and) Tj
T*
(removes access to the production environment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Scope) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Covers all production systems managed by Platform Operations, including application) Tj
T*
(servers, databases, and the container platform.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Requesting Access) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 Access requests are raised in the service desk tool. The data owner approves each access) Tj
T*
(request before the account is created.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 Permissions are granted according to the requester's job role. Each role grants only the) Tj
T*
(permissions that role requires to carry out its duties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 A shared ops-admin account is used by the on-call team for administrative tasks on) Tj
T*
(production servers. The account credentials are stored in the team password vault.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Authentication) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 Multi-factor authentication is enforced for VPN access to the corporate network.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Passwords must be at least eight characters in length.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 Credentials are never written into configuration files or source control. Secrets are) Tj
T*
(held in the platform secret store.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Access Review) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 The team lead reviews production access annually as part of the yearly compliance) Tj
T*
(exercise.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2 Review outcomes are noted in the compliance ticket.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
